Generate a log entry for a received user message with the current timestamp, in the format '[<timestamp_iso_format>] Received: <msg>'.

@param msg The user message received.

@return The log entry for the received message. Returns NULL on error (e.g., memory allocation failure, time conversion error, or NULL input message). The caller is responsible for freeing the returned memory.
*/
char* generate_receive_log(const char *msg) {
    // Safety check: Ensure the input message pointer is not NULL.
    // If msg is NULL, we cannot safely call strlen or snprintf with it.
    if (msg == NULL) {
